{"caption":"A rollout workflow turns success and failure traces into patches that are merged into an evolved skill.","description":"A left-to-right process diagram begins with a purple skill-like symbol beside crossed tools, labeled “Rollout Using Skills.” An arrow leads to a dashed rounded box labeled “Traces,” containing three rows. The green “Success Trace” says “Agent successfully matched rows across two sheets.” It carries a magenta T+ mark and a green circled check. The first red “Error Trace” says “MEDIAN(IF(xxx))” returned None in recalc.py; it carries a magenta T− mark and a red circled X. The second red “Error Trace” says “recalc.py” can’t handle excel array formulas; it also carries T− and a red circled X. Each row has a right-pointing arrow to a purple symbol marked in magenta A+ for the success row and A− for each error row, then another right-pointing arrow to its corresponding patch card.

A dashed rounded area titled “Patches” contains three cards. The green first card has an “Addition” icon and the heading “Patch1: add new pattern from success trace.” Its bullets read “Cast ID columns to str”; “Cast numeric columns to float before”; and “Cross-sheet row matching to prevent silent type-mismatch failures.” The red second card has an “Addition” icon and the heading “Patch2: add new warning from error trace.” Its bullets say “Array formulas silently fail in LibreOffice” and “Pre-calculate in Python and write the result as a literal value instead.” The red-bordered third card has an “Edition” icon and the heading “Patch3: Deepening existing rules from error trace.” Its bullets say “Use formulas, not hardcoded values.”; “Same rule, now with explicit text-function”; and “Add warning against auto-applying .strip”.

The first patch’s output line runs right and then down toward the merge; the second patch connects directly rightward; and the third patch’s output runs right and then up. All three feed into a purple merge symbol labeled “Merge Patches.” A right-pointing arrow leads from it to a crossed-tools symbol with a crown, labeled “Evolved Skill.”","figure_type":"diagram","chart_values":[]}
